# Compiled Hale binaries — produced by `hale build` next to source.
#
# Hale places the binary in the same directory as its main.hl, named
# after the directory (examples/<demo>/<demo>), plus sometimes a
# `main` binary from intermediate builds. CI / consumers should
# rebuild from .hl source.
#
# Generic rule: ignore everything under examples/, then un-ignore
# directories (so git can descend) and any file with an extension.
# Demo binaries are extensionless, so they stay ignored. NOTE: an
# extensionless *source* file (Procfile, Makefile) added under an
# examples/ dir must be force-added (`git add -f`) or given an
# explicit `!` rule here.
**/examples/**
!**/examples/**/
!**/examples/**/*.*

# Test binaries — `hale test` compiles to a temp dir, but the interim
# workaround for @ffi-linking tests (`hale test` skips the hale.toml
# [ffi] pickup, so sqlite/jobs/migrations tests are verified via
# `hale build <lib>/tests/<x>_test.hl` + run) drops extensionless
# binaries next to the test source. Same rule shape as examples/.
**/tests/**
!**/tests/**/
!**/tests/**/*.*

# Emitted intermediates. The examples/ rule above un-ignores anything
# with an extension so real sources stay tracked, which also lets
# compiler output (`--emit-llvm` and friends) slip through. These are
# build artifacts everywhere in the tree.
*.ll
*.o
*.s

# Library-root binaries (a CLI shape, e.g. migrations/migrations)
/migrations/migrations

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~

# Claude Code local settings — machine-specific, never commit
.claude/settings.local.json
